  <!-- The header of a profile's file (RealGlassProfiles\<name>.xml): one line per \n. -->
  <String key="File.ProfileHeader">
    Real Glass &amp; Water profile: a whole look, saved under the name of this file.\n
    \n
    Pick it at the top of the mod's in-game panel. The panel's Save button writes the look you
    have into this file; nothing else in the game changes it.\n
    \n
    - To share the look, copy this file into the RealGlassProfiles folder of another computer.
    Rename the file to rename the profile.\n
    - It holds every setting of the in-game panel's tabs. The settings that describe the computer
    (quality, language, keys, the button, the panels' look) are left out on purpose, and so are
    the glass mask view, the shore brush, each building asset's own glass (RealGlassAssets.xml)
    and a city's painted shores, which are kept in the city's save.\n
    - A setting missing from this file goes back to its default when the profile is picked.\n
    - The rules of RealGlass.xml apply here too: a dot for decimals, percentages written the way
    the slider shows them, a value out of range pulled back into it.\n
    - You can edit this file while the game is running. If it is the picked profile, the mod puts
    your edit in within a second of it being saved; otherwise the edit is used when you pick it.
    If it cannot be read at all, the mod leaves it alone and says so in the log.
  </String>

  <!-- ==================== The assets file (RealGlassAssets.xml) ==================== -->

  <!-- One line of the file per \n. -->
  <String key="AssetFile.Header">
    Real Glass &amp; Water: the glass each building asset has of its own, on every copy of it, in every
    city. Nothing of it is kept in your saves.\n
    \n
    One Asset element per asset, holding only what it does not take from RealGlass.xml, under
    the same names and in the same units:\n
    - a percentage the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%; GlassThreshold goes from 10 to 95
    (lower than in RealGlass.xml: it is this asset's alone);\n
    - GlassColor as #RRGGBB; GlassNightWindows, InteriorsEnabled, InteriorsCurtainsEnabled,
    InteriorsFollowIllumination and LodGlassFromModel as true or false (InteriorsCurtainsEnabled:
    curtains or blinds in its rooms, as many as InteriorsCurtains gives, or none;
    InteriorsFollowIllumination: its rooms lit where and when the game lights its windows, or as
    the Interiors tab says; LodGlassFromModel: its LOD shows the model's glass, or keeps its own);\n
    - GlassPreset as the number of a kind of glass (0 Custom, 1 to 10, as in RealGlass.xml);
    a kind of glass alone gives its color, reflectivity and clarity.\n
    \n
    One Prop element per prop made glass or water, on every copy of it: PropSurface Glass or
    Water, then any of GlassStrength, GlassPreset, GlassColor, GlassReflectivity, GlassClarity and
    GlassThreshold, as above (GlassThreshold from 0: all of the prop), and PropPolish (100 minus
    Frosted), PropWaterStrength, PropRippleStrength, PropRippleSize, PropRippleSpeed
    and PropSunGlint, in percent.\n
    \n
    The building window writes this file (press the building picker's key and click a
    building), and the prop window its props. You can edit it while the game is running too: the mod reads it again within a
    second. Take an asset's element out, or delete the file with the game closed, and it has
    the global glass again.
  </String>

  <!-- ==================== The creators' file (RealGlassDefinition.xml) ==================== -->

  <!-- Shipped with assets, beside their .crp. One line of the file per \n. -->
  <String key="CreatorFile.Header">
    Real Glass &amp; Water (Steam Workshop 3823419476): the glass of the building assets in this
    folder, as their creator set it, for every player who has the mod. A player's own settings
    for an asset (Alt+G) come first.\n
    \n
    One Asset element per asset, named by the asset's own name (as typed when saving it), holding
    only what its creator set: everything else follows each player's settings. The same names and
    units as RealGlassAssets.xml:\n
    - a percentage the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%; GlassThreshold goes from 10 to 95;\n
    - GlassColor as #RRGGBB; GlassNightWindows, InteriorsEnabled, InteriorsCurtainsEnabled,
    InteriorsFollowIllumination and LodGlassFromModel as true or false
    (InteriorsFollowIllumination: its rooms lit where and when the game lights its windows, as
    its illumination map says);\n
    - GlassPreset as the number of a kind of glass (0 Custom, 1 to 10).\n
    \n
    The asset editor writes this file when the asset is saved (set its glass in the creator
    window: the mod's key or button there), and puts it into the upload when the asset is
    shared from the Content Manager. Uploading another way, put this file beside the .crp.
  </String>

